          "Exact future-generation guidance restored; kept separate from “Become what we became, but greater.”"
        ],
        [
          "Pillar I — We Believe in People Before Problems\n\n“Every problem has a person behind it and a person in front of it.”\n\nWe refuse to allow the problem to become more visible than the person.\nA problem may demand our attention.\nA person deserves our compassion.\nWe listen to the person.\nWe strengthen the person.\nWe help resolve the problem.\nFor solving a problem without strengthening the person often allows the problem to return.\nStewardship begins and ends with people.\n\nReflection: “Am I helping solve a problem, or am I helping strengthen a person?”",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Pillar 1",
          "LOCKED — EXACT TEXT RECOVERED",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW; institutional posture; Steward training; institutional culture materials",
          "Internal / Stewards",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Institutional Posture Pillars",
          "Yes in THE SOUL OF AMW controlled text",
          "Founders / Legacy Council",
          "2026-09-02",
          "Exact pillar body and Reflection restored from the prior-chat institutional draft. Distinct from both the program/service-domain Seven Legacy Pillars and the separately controlled Legacy Charter Pillar VI."
        ],
        [
          "Pillar II — We Build Capacity, Not Dependency\n\nTrue assistance creates independence.\nTemporary relief has value.\nSustainable empowerment creates legacy.\nEvery service we provide should increase another person's ability to continue without us.\nOur greatest success is seeing someone discover they are capable of achieving more than they believed possible.\n\nReflection: “Did my help increase another person's confidence or only solve today's challenge?”",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Pillar 2",
          "LOCKED — EXACT TEXT RECOVERED",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW; institutional posture; Steward training; institutional culture materials",
          "Internal / Stewards",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Institutional Posture Pillars",
          "Yes in THE SOUL OF AMW controlled text",
          "Founders / Legacy Council",
          "2026-09-02",
          "Exact pillar body and Reflection restored from the prior-chat institutional draft. Distinct from both the program/service-domain Seven Legacy Pillars and the separately controlled Legacy Charter Pillar VI."
        ],
        [
          "Pillar III — We Give Credit Always\n\nRecognition belongs wherever contribution exists.\nSome contributions are visible.\nMany are not.\nWe honor both equally.\n\nEvery publication...\nEvery achievement...\nEvery partnership...\nEvery success story...\nEvery restored organization...\nEvery community initiative...\n\nExists because someone chose to contribute.\n\nWe celebrate every contribution, whether it receives applause or remains quietly behind the scenes.\nGratitude is stewardship made visible.\n\nReflection: “Whose contribution deserves recognition today?”",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Pillar 3",
          "LOCKED — EXACT TEXT RECOVERED",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW; institutional posture; Steward training; institutional culture materials",
          "Internal / Stewards",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Institutional Posture Pillars",
          "Yes in THE SOUL OF AMW controlled text",
          "Founders / Legacy Council",
          "2026-09-02",
          "Exact pillar body and Reflection restored from the prior-chat institutional draft. Distinct from both the program/service-domain Seven Legacy Pillars and the separately controlled Legacy Charter Pillar VI."
        ],
        [
          "Pillar IV — We Do Not Give Up\n\nNo challenge is too small to deserve our attention.\nNo challenge is too great to deserve our courage.\nWe approach every obstacle with hope, wisdom, perseverance, and humility.\nSometimes our strategy changes.\nSometimes our timeline changes.\nSometimes we ask others for help.\nBut we never stop believing that restoration is possible.\n\nReflection: “Where can I replace discouragement with determination today?”",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Pillar 4",
          "LOCKED — EXACT TEXT RECOVERED",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW; institutional posture; Steward training; institutional culture materials",
          "Internal / Stewards",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Institutional Posture Pillars",
          "Yes in THE SOUL OF AMW controlled text",
          "Founders / Legacy Council",
          "2026-09-02",
          "Exact pillar body and Reflection restored from the prior-chat institutional draft. Distinct from both the program/service-domain Seven Legacy Pillars and the separately controlled Legacy Charter Pillar VI."
        ],
        [
          "Pillar V — We Listen First\n\nListening is our first act of service.\nWe refuse to assume.\nWe seek to understand.\nOnly then do we advise.\nOnly then do we teach.\nOnly then do we lead.\nUnderstanding grows from listening.\nWisdom grows from understanding.\nService grows from wisdom.\n\nReflection: “Have I truly understood before offering my solution?”",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Pillar 5",
          "LOCKED — EXACT TEXT RECOVERED",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW; institutional posture; Steward training; institutional culture materials",
          "Internal / Stewards",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Institutional Posture Pillars",
          "Yes in THE SOUL OF AMW controlled text",
          "Founders / Legacy Council",
          "2026-09-02",
          "Exact pillar body and Reflection restored from the prior-chat institutional draft. Distinct from both the program/service-domain Seven Legacy Pillars and the separately controlled Legacy Charter Pillar VI."
        ],
        [
          "Pillar VI — We Leave Things Better\n\nThis is our promise.\n\nEvery relationship.\nEvery meeting.\nEvery neighborhood.\nEvery publication.\nEvery organization.\nEvery family.\nEvery child.\nEvery generation.\n\nShould become stronger because we were present.\n\nOur purpose is not merely to complete work.\nOur purpose is to leave strength behind.\n\nReflection: “Will what I leave today continue helping tomorrow?”",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Pillar 6",
          "LOCKED — EXACT TEXT RECOVERED",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW; institutional posture; Steward training; institutional culture materials",
          "Internal / Stewards",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Institutional Posture Pillars",
          "Yes in THE SOUL OF AMW controlled text",
          "Founders / Legacy Council",
          "2026-09-02",
          "Exact pillar body and Reflection restored from the prior-chat institutional draft. Distinct from both the program/service-domain Seven Legacy Pillars and the separately controlled Legacy Charter Pillar VI."
        ],
        [
          "Pillar VII — We Build for Tomorrow\n\nWe work for people we may never meet.\nChildren not yet born.\nCommunities not yet established.\nStewards not yet trained.\nLeaders not yet discovered.\nWe build today because tomorrow deserves preparation.\nLegacy is built through faithful work completed long before its full impact can be seen.\n\nReflection: “Would tomorrow thank me for the work I completed today?”",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW / Pillar 7",
          "LOCKED — EXACT TEXT RECOVERED",
          "THE SOUL OF AMW; institutional posture; Steward training; institutional culture materials",
